    "content": "# TrackFlow pricing proposal — Luna Cosmetics\n\n- **RFP reference:** RFP-E2E-33EC3E\n- **Ticket:** 33ec3e39-ec8d-44ee-9f4c-23a3d50d0c7c\n- **Currency:** USD\n- **Generated:** 2026-11-22T21:04:36.844852+00:00\n- **Proposal volume:** 4000 orders/month (capped by arbitration; the RFP asked for 5000)\n\n## Approvals\n\n| Department | Owner | Approved | Version |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Last Mile and Carrier Management | Carlos Vega | 2026-11-22T21:04:35.851058+00:00 | 2 |\n| Warehouse Operations | Ana Whitfield | 2026-11-22T21:03:42.781331+00:00 | 1 |\n\n## Resolved arbitration\n\n- **volume-vs-capacity** (árbitro: Miguel Torres): Limitar el volumen de la propuesta a la capacidad de warehouse (4000 pedidos/mes); lastmile revisa volumen y costo a la baja.\n\n## Last Mile and Carrier Management — Pricing proposal\n\n**Client:** Luna Cosmetics · **Country:** United States · **Currency:** USD · **TrackFlow owner:** Carlos Vega\n\n### Scope and approach\n\nThe cost to the customer includes shipping products across different regions of the country with a delivery SLA established to ensure timely deliveries. The provided data by the client is crucial for planning and execution, including monthly volume, USD pricing, and destination-specific delivery times.\n\n### Pricing items (USD)\n\n| Item | Price (USD) | Basis |\n|---|---|---|\n| Cost per shipment | To be quoted by Carlos Vega (final cost to the client) | By destination, weight and urgency; volume of 4000 orders/month. |\n| Available carriers | UPS, FedEx and DHL (Los Angeles) | The system picks the carrier by destination, weight and urgency. |\n| Delivery times | standard 3 to 5 business days within the same country; express 24 to 48 hours in metro areas (Los Angeles and Zaragoza-Madrid) | Same country. |\n\n### Volume discounts\n\n| Monthly volume | Discount on rate |\n|---|---|\n| Up to 2,000 orders/month | Pending approval by Miguel Torres |\n| 2,001 to 10,000 orders/month | Pending approval by Miguel Torres |\n| Over 10,000 orders/month | Pending approval by Miguel Torres |\n\n### Service level\n\n- On-time delivery SLA: **90 %** of deliveries on time per month, measured per country.\n- If a country falls below 90 % for two months in a row, we credit 5 % of that country's monthly fee.\n- On peak days, times can grow by up to 40 % and the SLA does not apply.\n\n### Assumptions and open questions\n\n- ¿Qué plazo de entrega esperan (estándar, express) y qué peso/tamaño medio tienen los paquetes?\n- ¿Cuál es el costo por envío para las diferentes regiones del US?\n\n## Warehouse Operations — Pricing proposal\n\n**Client:** Luna Cosmetics · **Country:** United States · **Currency:** USD · **TrackFlow owner:** Ana Whitfield\n\n### Scope and approach\n\nAlmacenamiento: Capacidad para el volumen/SKU del cliente; Tiempo de onboarding hasta operar. TrackFlow factura por m³ ocupado al mes, no por pallet ni por SKU. No hablemos de devoluciones, transporte ni última milla: los redactan Reverse Logistics y Last Mile.\n\n### Pricing items (USD)\n\n| Item | Price (USD) | Basis |\n|---|---|---|\n| Storage | 18 USD per m³ per month | Billed by occupied volume, not per unit. First 30 days free of charge. |\n| Long-term inventory | 150 % of the standard rate | From day 181 without movement. |\n| Cost per pallet / SKU | No per-unit rate: billed per m³ | The client did not state the SKU count. |\n| Capacity and onboarding | To be confirmed by Ana Whitfield | RFP volume: 5000 orders/month. RFP deadline: August 24th. |\n\n### Volume discounts\n\n| Monthly volume | Discount on rate |\n|---|---|\n| Up to 2,000 orders/month | Pending approval by Miguel Torres |\n| 2,001 to 10,000 orders/month | Pending approval by Miguel Torres |\n| Over 10,000 orders/month | Pending approval by Miguel Torres |\n\n### Service level\n\n- On-time delivery SLA: **90 %** of deliveries on time per month, measured per country.\n- If a country falls below 90 % for two months in a row, we credit 5 % of that country's monthly fee.\n- On peak days, times can grow by up to 40 % and the SLA does not apply.\n\n### Assumptions and open questions\n\n- ¿Cuál es el costo por pallet/SKU?\n"
  }
